Methods and getset functions with the parameters CPython calls them with: a getter takes a
closure, a setter a value and a closure, a METH_NOARGS method an (unused) second argument, a
METH_VARARGS|METH_KEYWORDS one its (unused) keywords.
Natively a call with more arguments than the function takes goes unnoticed; WebAssembly checks
the type of every indirect call, and the guest's CPython (no Emscripten trampoline) traps:
copy.copy(np.float64(1)), arr.dtype = ... and the others ended the interpreter (and a
METH_VARARGS function of the test module took keywords it never had).
(Found by the add-on's tools/fpcast-scan.py.)

